# balena/devices/Dockerfile.tailscale — the VS devices fleet's tailscale
# overlay service image (fleet-ops-j7g.1: the served agent origin — the
# owner-decided serve form for the AC3 live leg).
#
# The devices fleet's tailscale service JOINED only through devices-v1.1.0
# (stock pinned image, serves nothing — the lnf master/devices delta).
# This build promotes it to the devices' own SERVE edge for exactly ONE
# surface: the agent's A2A origin (:9900), which the master gateway's
# proxy dials to deliver peer traffic. Same serve-only TLS edge pattern
# as the master's lnf build (Dockerfile.tailscale in balena/registrar):
# ACLs govern access, TLS auto-provisioned, identity headers intact,
# zero new firewall surface — the origin is published at the device's
# own MagicDNS name, never at a host port.
#
# THE ${TS_CERT_DOMAIN} PLACEHOLDER (unlike the master's literal bake):
# the devices fleet is N devices from ONE compose — a literal FQDN
# cannot serve every node. containerboot substitutes ${TS_CERT_DOMAIN}
# with the node's own cert domain at apply time (cmd/containerboot/
# serve.go readServeConfig: bytes.ReplaceAll(j, []byte("${TS_CERT_DOMAIN}"),
# []byte(certDomain)) — verified at the pinned v1.102.5 tag), and on a
# non-kube node the cert domain is the node's own MagicDNS FQDN (the
# netmap's st.CertDomains[0] — main.go nmState.certDomains.At(0); the
# live master proves the field non-empty: its serve config applied and
# Let's Encrypt certificates issued). Each device therefore serves its
# A2A origin at https://<device>.tailb7207e.ts.net:9900 with its own LE
# certificate — provisioned the same way the master's are, no owner
# step beyond the tailnet-wide HTTPS enable already in place (lnf).
#
# Dialect note (same as the master's build — verified from the pinned
# image's own source, v1.102.5, cmd/containerboot/serve.go
# readServeConfig): TS_SERVE_CONFIG is a raw ipn.ServeConfig JSON file.
#   TCP  — map keyed by PORT number ("9900"), value { "HTTPS": true }
#   Web  — map keyed "SNI:port" (no implicit 443 in this dialect), each
#          a Handlers map keyed by mount point, "/" proxying the
#          loopback publish of the agent service (127.0.0.1:9900 —
#          tailscaled runs in the host network namespace where compose
#          names don't resolve, the same reason the master's serve
#          config proxies loopback).
# The apply is REFUSED with a logged refusal line when the tailnet has
# HTTPS certificates disabled; the owner prerequisite (admin console →
# MagicDNS → HTTPS Certificates) has been live since lnf — the master's
# own cert lines are the primary-source proof.
# A file change re-applies via fsnotify (with a 5s-ticker fallback), so
# the baked bytes are also the recovery path after any drift.

FROM tailscale/tailscale:v1.102.5

COPY serve-config.json /serve-config.json